 646	/// The exact directed extreme of a stream of ratios num/den (both exact), in
 647	/// memory that does not depend on the stream (KF1).
 648	///
 649	/// A row counts while its 64-bit approximation (its key, compared as a bit
 650	/// pattern) lies within `WINDOW_ULPS` of the running approximate extreme,
 651	/// exactly as K4's tracker kept it; `finish` returns the directed extreme of
 652	/// the exact ratios of the rows that count, or the refusal of the earliest of
 653	/// them whose exact evaluation refuses, bit for bit as K4's did.
 654	///
 655	/// At most T rows are held unevaluated. A collapse evaluates them exactly and
 656	/// keeps (key, outcome) entries, pruned to those that no entry nearer the best
 657	/// key (larger for Up, smaller for Down) with an outcome that decides `finish`
 658	/// at least as early dominates. The window removes rows by key alone, and a
 659	/// dominating entry's key is nearer the best, so it outlasts every row it
 660	/// dominates: the result is the same for any collapse schedule (KF1 plan §2).
 661	pub(crate) struct BoundedExtremeTracker {
 662	    direction: Direction,
 663	    limit: usize,
 664	    best: Option<u64>,
 665	    offered: u64,
 666	    /// Unevaluated rows: (num, den, key, place in the stream).
 667	    lazy: Vec<(ExactWideSum, ExactWideSum, u64, u64)>,
 668	    /// Evaluated entries (key, outcome), nearest the best first.
 669	    table: Vec<(u64, Evaluated)>,
 670	}
